ana: opened a tiny docs PR adding a short 'envelope' vs bare call example + a parsing shim for nullable lists. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5073

chris: can we show both patterns side-by-side and a single 6-7 line SDK helper that demonstrates a deterministic error text? tests rely on exact strings.

mai: also include a one-liner to normalize single-object -> array and null -> [] for `items` 1 practical.

ana: draft examples: bare call:
```json
{"name":"get_order","arguments":{"order_id":"ord_7"}}
```

envelope suggestion (preferred when adding metadata):
```json
{"call":{"name":"get_order","arguments":{"order_id":"ord_7"}},"meta":{"svc":"orders","ver":"2025-07-01"}}
```

chris: prefer short key `meta` not `metadata`. add tiny guardrail note: prefer tolerating extra fields for forward-compatibility (`"additionalProperties": true`).

sam: SDK helper I added to the PR (7 lines):
```js
try {
  const out = parseStructured(resp, schema);
  return out;
} catch (e) {
  throw new Error("StructuredParseError: missing required field 'order_id'");
}
```

mai: exact error string looks good. for nullable-lists shim use:
```js
const items = Array.isArray(res.items) ? res.items : (res.items ? [res.items] : []);
```

this is compact and covers both single-object and null cases.

